## Example Usage

{{ tffile "examples/resources/baseten_secret/resource.tf" }}

## Rotating a value

`value_wo` is never stored, so editing it alone produces no plan diff. Increment
`value_wo_version` in the same commit:

```terraform
resource "baseten_secret" "hf_access_token" {
  name             = "hf_access_token"
  value_wo         = var.hf_access_token
  value_wo_version = 2
}
```

The secret's `id` is stable across rotation.

## Ordering against models that read it

A model names its secrets in `config.yaml`, which Terraform cannot see, so no
dependency edge is inferred. Declare it:

```terraform
resource "baseten_secret" "hf_access_token" {
  name             = "hf_access_token"
  value_wo         = var.hf_access_token
  value_wo_version = 1
}

resource "baseten_model" "llama" {
  name = "Llama 3.2 1B"

  push = {
    config_dir = "${path.module}/llama"
  }

  depends_on = [baseten_secret.hf_access_token]
}
```

Where `llama/config.yaml` reads:

```yaml
model_name: Llama 3.2 1B
secrets:
  hf_access_token: null
```

## Team-scoped secrets

Team secrets are stored separately from the workspace's own, so a model outside
the team cannot read one.

```terraform
resource "baseten_secret" "hf_access_token" {
  name = "hf_access_token"

  # Or team_id, if you have it. Set neither for the default team.
  team_name = "research"

  value_wo         = var.hf_access_token
  value_wo_version = 1
}
```

`baseten_model` takes the same pair, and model names are unique only within a
team, so set one there too when resolving a model by name.

## Destroying

`deletion_protection` defaults to true, because a deleted secret cannot be
recovered and every model reading it breaks. A `terraform destroy` reads the
flag out of state, so turn it off and apply before destroying:

```terraform
resource "baseten_secret" "hf_access_token" {
  deletion_protection = false
}
```

